<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Ceval director dies in car crash.</title>
<headline>Brazil Ceval director dies in car crash.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polidorio Osmar Ferreira, director of the Industrial Products Division at Brazilian food processor Ceval Alimentos SA, died on November 30 in a car accident, a Ceval spokesman said.</p>
<p>Ferreira, 44, joined Ceval in 1978 and was made a director in 1986. One of his responsibilities had been the purchase of soybeans from overseas, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>Ferreira, who is survived by his wife and four children, was buried December 1 in Itajai, southern Brazil, where he was born.</p>
<p>There has so far been no announcement as to who will now assume Ferreira's position, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>-- Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151</p>
</text>
